=================
*httk* quickstart
=================

Install
-------

Install the ``httk2`` metapackage from a local checkout or from PyPI:

.. code:: bash

     git clone https://github.com/httk/httk2.git
     pip install ./httk2

.. code:: bash

     pip install httk2

Either way this installs the complete standard set of httk₂ modules with their
recommended default features. Developers can instead track the latest
development state of all modules via the metapackage's ``dev-main`` branch and
its Makefile helpers; see the
`httk2 README <https://github.com/httk/httk2#readme>`__ for details.

Try it out
----------

* Quickstarts covering specific functionalities are available for working with:

  - `Atomic structures (i.e., crystal structures / slabs / molecules) <quickstart-structures.html>`__
  - `Vectors <quickstart-vectors.html>`__
  - `UI and websites <quickstart-httk-serve.html>`__
  - `Databases <quickstart-databases.html>`__

* The full documentation includes `example notebooks
  <https://docs.httk.org/dev/main/notebooks/>`__ and a `step-by-step tutorial
  <https://docs.httk.org/dev/main/tutorial/>`__.
